;; Go-build variant of java.net.DatagramSocket (J2G-SPEC §4.6; doc/go/JRT-NOTES.md, "Datagrams"; F10 of
;; doc/classes/JAVA-DEFERRED-TRIAGE.md, "As built: F10b"): read by j2g only. Since F10b a datagram socket's
;; delegate is jdk26u's (createDelegate unchanged: the NIO adaptor, sun.nio.ch.DatagramSocketAdaptor over
;; DatagramChannelImpl, else a DatagramSocketImplFactory's impl in the legacy NetMulticastSocket); F11's
;; replacement of createDelegate (the legacy delegate over HostDatagramSocketImpl always) is gone. The variant
;; only adds jrtNoDelegate, NO_DELEGATE for the adaptor, which jdk26u reads through a private lookup's VarHandle
;; (java.lang.invoke's lookups are not in the Go build). Copyright (c) the Arbace authors; Eclipse Public
;; License 1.0.
(in-ns 'java.net)

(j2g/variant DatagramSocket
  (j2g/add
    (method ^:public ^:static jrtNoDelegate ^SocketAddress []
      NO_DELEGATE)))
